- [Development of a 1.5 µm Resolution Digital Lithography System](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0605_01.html): Nikon is developing a high-productivity digital lithography system for advanced packaging processes in semiconductor manufacturing back-end operations, delivering 1.5 μm resolution (L/S) while targeting more than a 30% improvement in throughput—from 50 panels per hour with the DSP-100 digital lithography system to 65 panels per hour or higher with the new system.  The new system is scheduled for release in fiscal year 2027.
- [Selected for Dow Jones Best-in-Class World Index for the 8th Consecutive Year](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0520_01.html): Nikon has been selected for the eighth consecutive year as a component of the World Index and the Asia Pacific Index within the Dow Jones Best-in-Class Indices, a globally recognized ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) investment benchmark.  Nikon has also been selected for all ESG indices adopted by the Government Pension Investment Fund (GPIF) targeting domestic stocks.
- [Nikon's telescopes to be installed on Axelspace's next-generation Earth observation satellites “GRUS-3”](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0519_01.html): Nikon is pleased to announce that its telescopes will be installed on seven GRUS‑3, the next‑generation Earth observation microsatellites developed by Axelspace Corporation (Axelspace), a pioneer of microsatellites that has been leading the space business.  These telescopes, when combined with Axelspace’s image sensor units, feature a compact structure while enabling acquisition of high‑resolution images with stable quality. The GRUS‑3 satellites equipped with Nikon’s telescopes are scheduled to be launched no earlier than July 2026.
- [Nikon is developing the NIKKOR Z 120-300mm f/2.8 TC VR S, a telephoto zoom lens with a built-in 1.4x teleconverter](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0507_imaging_01.html): Nikon is developing the NIKKOR Z 120-300mm f/2.8 TC VR S, a telephoto zoom lens for full-frame/FX-format mirrorless cameras. Part of the NIKKOR Z lens S-Line, it features a built-in 1.4× teleconverter and covers a focal-length range of 120mm to 420mm. Combining outstanding optical performance with high mobility, it supports professional image-making, including sports photography.
- [Received Highest MSCI ESG Rating of AAA for the Fourth Consecutive Year | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0428_01.html): Nikon has received the highest "AAA" rating in the MSCI ESG Ratings for four consecutive years. In 2026, Nikon was recognized for its initiatives in areas such as conflict minerals and corporate governance. In addition, Nikon has been selected as a constituent of all domestic equity ESG indices adopted by the Government Pension Investment Fund (GPIF). 
- [Nikon releases the new APDIS MV5X Laser Radar | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0420_01.html): Nikon Corporation has launched the APDIS MV5X, the latest addition to its APDIS Laser Radar product lineup. Building on the proven technologies of previous APDIS models, the APDIS MV5X delivers high-speed, high-precision non-contact measurement in a compact and lightweight form, enhancing the quality of the manufacturing process.
- [Live Cell Observation System Selected for NASA-Supported Project Heading to the International Space Station | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0407_02.html): A live-cell imaging system developed by Nikon and its U.S. subsidiary, Nikon Instruments Inc. (NII), has been selected for a NASA-supported project and will be deployed aboard the International Space Station (ISS). The mission will conduct initial operational verification of a microscope system used for culturing, maintaining, and observing live cells and tissues. Nikon will contribute to research on the effects of microgravity in drug discovery.
- [Message from the CEO on the Start of a New Management Structure | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0401_01.html): Yasuhiro Ohmura assumed the position of Representative Director, President and CEO of Nikon on 1 April 2026, marking the start of a new management structure. This page features a message from Ohmura on the occasion of his appointment.
- [Nikon CeLL Innovation to Provide End-to-End Solutions from Process Development to GCTP/GMP Manufacturing and Analytical Characterization of Human Mesenchymal Stem Cells and Extracellular Vesicles in Japan | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0312_01.html): Nikon's subsidiary, Nikon CeLL innovation Co., Ltd. (NCLi), has completed the commercial-scale technology transfer of manufacturing processes for human mesenchymal stromal cells (MSCs) and extracellular vesicles (EVs) from RoosterBio, Inc. This enables NCLi to provide comprehensive solutions in Japan, from process development to GCTP- and GMP-compliant manufacturing and analysis for MSCs and EVs.
- [Nikon's Spatial Omics Analysis Software Technology to be Utilized in Joint Research on Breast Cancer Metastasis Led by the University of Tokyo | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0304_01.html): Software technology developed by Nikon that visualizes multiple layers of spatial omics data on microscope images was used in a collaborative research project led by Professor Yutaka Suzuki and colleagues at the Graduate School of Frontier Sciences, The University of Tokyo. The technology supports the analysis and interpretation of breast cancer metastasis.
- [Nikon Announces Investment in U.S.-based Vast, Inc. | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0306_01.html): Nikon has invested in Vast, Inc., a US company developing commercial space stations. Vast designs, develops, manufactures, and operates commercial space stations using a vertically integrated manufacturing approach. The company aims for its next-generation commercial space station to serve as a successor to the International Space Station (ISS) following its planned retirement in 2030.Nikon aims to expand its business in the aerospace sector across a range of fields, including its additive manufacturing (AM) business, which is positioned as a growth driver in the current Medium-Term Management Plan, as well as its imaging business.
- [Nikon Announces Investment in Trener Robotics | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0213_01.html): Nikon has invested in US-based Trener Robotics (CEO: Asad Tirmizi) through the NFocus Fund. Trener Robotics provides Acteris, a platform that enables AI-powered natural language programming for industrial robots. Through this investment, Nikon will combine Trener Robotics' advanced digital technologies with its own robot vision systems to deliver solutions that support the next generation of automated and labor-efficient manufacturing.
- [Selected for the highest rank, “A List,” in the CDP's climate change survey for the seventh consecutive year | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2026/0119_01.html): Nikon was named to CDP's Climate Change A List for the seventh consecutive year in recognition of its climate change initiatives and disclosure efforts. In addition, Nikon received an A- rating in CDP's Water Security assessment for the second consecutive year.The Nikon Group continues to contribute to building a sustainable society through its Nikon Long-Term Environmental Vision, which comprises three pillars: "Realizing a Decarbonized Society," "Realizing a Resource Circulating Society," and "Realizing a Healthy and Environmentally Safe Society." In addressing climate change, the Nikon Group aims to achieve carbon neutrality across its entire supply chain by fiscal year 2050.
- [Nikon Introduces the Litho Booster 1000, a Next-Generation Alignment Station Designed to Facilitate Breakthrough Overlay Accuracy for Advanced 3D Devices | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2025/1211_01.html): Nikon is developing the Litho Booster 1000, the latest model in its alignment station lineup. The system measures wafers before the lithography process and feeds correction data to lithography systems to achieve high overlay accuracy. The Litho Booster 1000 is scheduled for release in the second half of 2026. Alignment stations are compatible with both Nikon and third-party semiconductor lithography systems, and Nikon has offered them since 2018. By maintaining high productivity while enabling highly accurate multi-point absolute measurements, the Litho Booster 1000 aims to improve manufacturing yield.
- [Launch of “S3S LAB”, a Co-Creation Platform Equipped with Roll-to-Roll Maskless Lithography System | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2025/1210_01.html): On December 10, 2025, Nikon opened S3S LAB, a Co-Creation Platform located at its Sagamihara Plant in Kanagawa Prefecture, and commenced operations. S3S LAB is equipped with a comprehensive range of equipment required for flexible electronics development, including Nikon’s proprietary state-of-the-art Roll-to-Roll (R2R) Maskless Exposure System and peripheral equipment incorporating advanced film deposition and multilayer wiring technologies for device manufacturing. Serving as a new hub for innovation, S3S LAB supports customers from research and development through commercialization.
- [Nikon Begins Accepting Orders for the FX-88SL and FX-88SLD, the First FPD Lithography Systems Equipped with UV-LED Light Source | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2025/1023_01.html): Nikon will begin accepting orders in November 2025 for the FX-88SL and FX-88SLD, Gen 8 plate (2,290 mm × 2,620 mm) FPD lithography systems. As the first FPD lithography systems to incorporate a UV-LED (ultraviolet LED) light source, the FX-88SL and FX-88SLD deliver high resolution and high productivity while reducing environmental impact.
- [Nikon releases the ZR, a full-frame sensor camera from the "Z CINEMA" series born from synergy with RED](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2025/0910_imaging_01.html): The ZR features the R3D NE video recording file format, developed based on RED's RAW codec, and inherits RED color science and exposure standards to enable highly accurate color matching with RED cameras. Supporting up to 6K recording, a 15+ stop dynamic range, and Dual Base ISO settings of ISO 800 and ISO 6400, it enables high-quality video production even in low-light environments.In addition, the ZR offers 32-bit float audio recording, high-quality audio capture powered by OZO Audio, a lightweight body weighing approximately 540 g, and a 4.0-inch monitor, balancing portability with professional-quality performance.The product reflects Nikon's strategy to strengthen its presence in the high-end video production market, including film production.
- [Orders Begin in July for Digital Lithography System DSP-100 | News | Nikon About Us](https://www.nikon.com/company/news/2025/0716_01.html): Nikon began accepting orders for the DSP-100 digital lithography system in July 2025. Designed for advanced packaging in semiconductor device manufacturing, the DSP-100 combines 1.0 μm (L/S) resolution with support for large substrates up to 600 mm square.
